\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs24  \plain \f1\fs24 (ff. 4r-103v) Catena in Pauli epistulam ad Romanos (Ms. ohne Titel), ed. \plain \f2\scaps\lang1033\fs24 J. A. Cramer\plain \f1\fs24 , Catenae graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, IV, Oxford 1844 (Ndr. Hildesheim 1967), S. 163-529; CPG C 161. - Katene vom \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs24 Typus Monacensis,\plain \f1\fs24 dessen Haupthandschrift Cod. graec. Monac. 412 ist, vgl. \plain \f2\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Staab \plain \f1\fs24 (\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs24 Lit\plain \f1\fs24 ). Breitkatene (Typ II \plain \f2\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Karo - Lietzmann\plain \f1\fs24 ). Bibeltext durch Einr\u252 \'fccken am linken Rand vom Kommentartext getrennt. Angabe von Kapitel und Versen am Rand. Am Beginn der Kapitel f. 31r und f. 88r: \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs24 Caput VIII\plain \f1\fs24 bzw. \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs24 Caput IX \plain \f1\fs24 in Rot. - Genannt werden folgende Autoren: \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Acacius\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Caesariensis\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Apollinaris\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Laodicenus\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Basilius\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Caesariensis\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Caesarius\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Clemens\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Alexandrinus\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Cyrillus\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Alexandrinus\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Didymus\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Caecus\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Diodorus\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Tarsensis\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Dionysius\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Alexandrinus\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Dionysius \plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Areopagita\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Euthalius\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Gennadius\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Gregorius\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Nazianzenus\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Gregorius\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Nyssenus\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Ioannes Chrysostomus\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Ioannes Damascenus\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Isidorus\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Maximus\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Confessor\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Methodius\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Oecumenius\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Origenes\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Photius\plain \f1\fs24 , \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Severianus\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Gabalensis\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Theodoretus\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Cyrensis\plain \f1\fs24 >, \plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Theodorus\plain \f1\fs24 <\plain \f2\b\lang1033\fs24 Mopsuestenus\plain \f1\fs24 >. - (ff. 4r-30r) Rom. 7, 7-25. - (ff. 31r-87v) 8, 1-39. - (ff. 88r-103v) 9, 1-13; \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs24 des. mut. \plain \f2\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Cramer,\plain \f1\fs24 S. 333, 19 \plain \f4\lang1032\fs24 \u949 \'e5\u7984 ?\u962 \'f2 \u959 \'ef\u7990 ?\u954 \'ea\u959 \'ef\u957 \'ed \u922 \'ca\u965 \'f5\u961 \'f1\u8055 ?\u959 \'ef\u965 \'f5 \u960 \'f0\u959 \'ef\u961 \'f1\u949 \'e5\u965 \'f5\u963 \'f3\u8057 ?\u956 \'ec\u949 \'e5\u952 \'e8\u945 \'e1.}

